diff --git a/docs/env_switches.tsv b/docs/env_switches.tsv
index 527c3676..b427084e 100644
--- a/docs/env_switches.tsv
+++ b/docs/env_switches.tsv
@@ -206,6 +206,7 @@ DM_PROBE_LIMIT	diagnostic	Maximum printed hits per guest probe; 0 or absent leav
 DM_PROBE_POLL	diagnostic	`=<address>[+<length>]` (hex, 4 bytes by default, up to 8): a host thread spins on the bytes and on each change snapshots every thread's pc, lr and frames, for writes the watch misses
 DM_PROBE_WATCH	diagnostic	`=<address>[+<length>]` (hex, 8 bytes by default): write-protects that host page and reports who writes these bytes, without a debugger
 DM_PROBE_X2	diagnostic	`=<bytes>` (hex): probe hits also dump that many bytes of the memory x2 points to
+DM_PROFILE	path	`=<file>`: the runtime game profile (layout, switches, tables) the host reads at start, which is how one host binary serves every game (the launcher architecture); the compiled `game_profile.h` stays the fallback, and `DM_PROF_<key>` overrides sit on top of it (`hle_profile.h`)
 DM_PROGRAM_ID	switch	`=<hex>`: the program ID the host reports from `svcGetInfo(ProgramId)` (default: the profile's `program_id`)
 DM_PSO_ARCHIVE	path	The folder of the per-game Metal 4 pipeline archive of pipeline bases (default `pso_archive/` beside `pso_user.tsv`); `off` keeps no archive
 DM_PSO_BUNDLE	path	The pipeline archive made offline (`<GPU architecture>.mtl4a`, `prebuilt.tsv`), read only; the iOS app and Mac launcher set it to their `pso/` folder; `off` ignores it
